lib:F0201 a crgo:CRGO_0000024 ;
    rdfs:label "Lack of secure message queues for system integration"@en ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000196 lib:F0201-event ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000246 theme:ThemeAppSec ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000250 "LIB-F0201" ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000287 "combined_file.xlsx rows R0609" ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000322 crgo:CRGO_0000306 ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000329 "healthcare" ;
    crgo:CRGO_0000330 "Access Controls: Implement strong access controls to restrict access to the message queues only to authorized personnel and systems"@en,
        "Encryption: Encrypt the messages and data stored within the message queues to protect them from unauthorized access or tampering"@en,
        "Implement Secure Message Queuing: Deploy a secure message queuing system that ensures the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of sensitive data transferred between systems"@en,
        "Monitoring and Logging: Implement monitoring and logging mechanisms to detect any unusual activity or potential attacks on the message queues, and set up alerts to notify the security team"@en,
        "Regular Updates and Patching: Keep the message queuing system and associated software up to date with the latest security patches and updates to mitigate known vulnerabilities"@en,
        "Risk Scenario: Lack of secure message queues for system integration Summary: The lack of secure message queues for system integration in a healthcare organization can result in unauthorized access, data breaches, and disruption of critical services. Mitigation Measures"@en .

