    crgo:CRGO_0000330 "Continuous monitoring: Deploy an Intrusion Detection System (IDS) or Intrusion Prevention System (IPS) to detect and prevent any suspicious activities"@en,
        "Description: The hospital's network infrastructure uses insecure protocols, which can be exploited by attackers to intercept and manipulate sensitive data in transit. Mitigation Measures"@en,
        "Regular patch management: Ensure network devices and software are updated with the latest security patches to address known vulnerabilities"@en,
        "Risk Scenario"@en,
        "Title: Insecure network protocols enabling man-in-the-middle attacks"@en,
        "Upgrade network protocols: Implement secure communication protocols such as Transport Layer Security (TLS) or Internet Protocol Security (IPsec) to encrypt and authenticate network communications"@en .

