        "Description: This scenario involves the accidental or unintended disclosure of sensitive data by internal staff members at the organisation"@en,
        "Estimated CVSS (Common Vulnerability Scoring System) Score: Calculating the CVSS score requires detailed information about the vulnerability being assessed, including its impact, exploitability, and other factors. Without this information, it is not possible to provide an accurate estimate"@en,
        "Expected Utility: The expected utility relates to the strategic importance of the assets involved in the scenario. Without specific knowledge of the hospital's assets and priorities, it is challenging to provide an accurate estimate. However, a reasonable starting point could be 0.8 (80%)"@en,
        "Maximal Damages: The maximal damages represent the worst-case scenario and would depend on the extent and impact of the data leak. Again, without knowing specific details, it is difficult to provide an accurate estimate. However, a reasonable starting point could be 0.9 (90%)"@en,
        "Mitigation Measures"@en .

